caption: Champions

Gods and demons can both designate Champions. This costs 22 character points: 20 to pay for the class they get, which you choose, and 1 point to pay for the mind link, coming and going. Champions don’t have to agree to become your champion, and you don’t have to tell them anything, but usually it is more productive to have will-informed champions that agree to take the job. Champions are broken free from the restrictive class system, allowing them to take classes beyond their species allowed once they have mastered one, and to invest in their Ordained class. A character can only be a champion of a single god. Champions wielding a weapon given to them by their god or demon lord counts as sacrificing everyone they kill to their patron.

Champions can change who they serve simply by choosing a new god, and that god spending two experience to create the mind-link. This cannot be done without the Champion’s consent, and does not give them access to an additional class, though they can gain new classes as normal.
